WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.602
Welcome to the OurWater map.

00:00:02.722 --> 00:00:07.426
You will learn to find stations, filter them
by kind and by distance,

00:00:07.546 --> 00:00:13.594
search for a place or for GPS numbers, and
save a group of stations as a monitoring area.

00:00:14.417 --> 00:00:17.153
Open the map from the menu on the left.

00:00:17.273 --> 00:00:21.521
The number at the bottom tells you how many
stations you can see right now.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.422
The first chip chooses whose stations you see.

00:00:25.542 --> 00:00:29.646
My stations shows only the wells and gauges
you look after.

00:00:29.766 --> 00:00:34.230
All stations shows everyone's, so you can see
who measures near you.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.794
Stations that are close together merge into a
round bubble.

00:00:38.914 --> 00:00:41.890
The number is how many stations it holds.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:44.074
Tap a bubble to zoom in.

00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:47.667
Now each station is its own pin.

00:00:47.787 --> 00:00:53.499
The picture shows its kind: a well, a
borewell, a rain gauge or a check-dam.

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:55.971
A red ring means it is yours.

00:00:56.783 --> 00:01:02.831
Tap a pin and a card opens with the station's
name, kind, code and coordinates.

00:01:02.951 --> 00:01:09.095
Its buttons add a measurement, show the details or
history, draw a chart, or save a favourite.

00:01:09.917 --> 00:01:15.701
Station details shows what we know: the
village, your remark, the last measurement,

00:01:15.821 --> 00:01:17.813
and the kinds of measurement.

00:01:18.617 --> 00:01:24.761
The Chart tab draws the measurements as a line, so
you can see whether the water is rising or falling.

00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:30.239
History lists the latest measurements with
date, kind and value.

00:01:30.359 --> 00:01:32.855
Open full history shows them all.

00:01:33.683 --> 00:01:35.987
Down the left are the map tools.

00:01:36.107 --> 00:01:38.195
Plus and minus zoom.

00:01:38.315 --> 00:01:43.859
The frame button fits all your stations on the
screen, so you can always find your way back.

00:01:44.683 --> 00:01:48.715
The target button finds where you are, if your
device allows it.

00:01:48.835 --> 00:01:51.979
A blue dot marks you, and the map moves there.

00:01:52.783 --> 00:01:54.655
Tap the search bar.

00:01:54.775 --> 00:02:00.607
Type a station's name or code, a village or
town, or even GPS numbers.

00:02:01.417 --> 00:02:05.545
Type part of a name or code, and matching
stations appear.

00:02:05.665 --> 00:02:10.321
All four practice codes start with T U T, so
all four match.

00:02:10.441 --> 00:02:13.009
Choose one and the map flies to it.

00:02:13.817 --> 00:02:15.857
A place name works too.

00:02:15.977 --> 00:02:19.505
Under Places you see matching villages and
towns.

00:02:19.625 --> 00:02:22.025
Choose one as your reference point.

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.658
The map flies there and drops a red pin.

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:27.986
Distances are measured from it.

00:02:28.817 --> 00:02:33.641
GPS numbers work too: latitude first, then
longitude.

00:02:33.761 --> 00:02:37.385
OurWater offers that exact spot as a reference
point.

00:02:38.217 --> 00:02:41.529
Radius asks: which stations are near here?

00:02:41.649 --> 00:02:44.193
The Location line shows the centre.

00:02:44.313 --> 00:02:48.633
You can also use your own location, or tap a
spot on the map.

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:52.690
Choose a distance, such as five kilometres.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:57.634
A sentence tells you how many stations are
inside: here, all four.

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:00.322
Or slide the bar.

00:03:00.442 --> 00:03:04.186
At one kilometre, only two stations are
inside.

00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:08.233
Close the sheet and the map draws a green
circle.

00:03:08.353 --> 00:03:12.025
The number at the bottom counts only the
stations inside it.

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:18.082
Clear all removes every filter at once: the
distance, and the red pin too.

00:03:18.883 --> 00:03:22.075
Open Type to choose the kinds of station you
want.

00:03:22.195 --> 00:03:25.435
The number beside each is how many there are.

00:03:25.555 --> 00:03:30.307
Tick a kind, and the button below shows how
many stations will appear.

00:03:31.117 --> 00:03:32.989
Press Show.

00:03:33.109 --> 00:03:37.045
The map keeps only that kind, and the chip
shows its name.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:43.490
A monitoring area is a group of stations you
watch together, like the wells in one village.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.226
Saved areas are in this list.

00:03:46.346 --> 00:03:49.586
This account has one: Badgaon village.

00:03:50.417 --> 00:03:55.073
To make a new one, open Actions and choose
Create a Monitoring Area.

00:03:55.193 --> 00:04:00.977
A panel opens with three tools: pick stations,
drag a box, or draw a shape.

00:04:01.783 --> 00:04:04.327
Choose Pick stations and tap one.

00:04:04.447 --> 00:04:07.039
It joins your list, top right.

00:04:07.159 --> 00:04:10.351
For now, the map hides the other stations.

00:04:11.183 --> 00:04:15.407
Tick Show other stations to bring them back,
then tap two more.

00:04:15.527 --> 00:04:18.119
The cross beside a name removes it.

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:23.750
Press Save, and type a name you will remember,
like My village wells.

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:26.422
Press Save again.

00:04:26.542 --> 00:04:30.502
The area is saved, and the first chip shows
its name.

00:04:31.317 --> 00:04:35.181
You can keep ten areas, with thirty stations
in each.

00:04:35.301 --> 00:04:40.053
At ten, Save shows this message: delete one to
add another.

00:04:40.883 --> 00:04:44.987
To delete an area, open the list and tap the
bin beside it.

00:04:45.107 --> 00:04:47.099
Press Delete to confirm.

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:51.203
The area goes, but your stations and
measurements stay.

00:04:52.017 --> 00:04:56.289
Choose Badgaon village, and the map shows just
its stations.

00:04:56.409 --> 00:04:59.289
A new chart button appears down the left.

00:04:59.409 --> 00:05:05.457
Press it to continue with the area: its data
opens as a Data trend or as Data statistics.

00:05:06.283 --> 00:05:11.611
Choose Data trend, and the chart opens with
Badgaon village already selected.

00:05:12.417 --> 00:05:14.361
That is the whole page.

00:05:14.481 --> 00:05:19.137
You can replay this tutorial any time from the
Learning page inside the app.

00:05:19.257 --> 00:05:21.921
Thanks for helping look after our water.
